<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodoric II, King of the Visigoths</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 466</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-ii">Theodoric II</a> was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 453 to 466, after murdering his brother Thorismund. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> as a Roman ally, he helped make <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avitus">Avitus</a> emperor in 455 and in 456 crushed the Suebi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, killing their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rechiar">Rechiar</a>. He extended Visigothic power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and Hispania before being murdered by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euric">Euric</a>.</p></div>
